---
description: Prefer minimal comments; short godoc on exports; no narrating blocks
alwaysApply: true
---

# Minimal comments

Comment only when the code cannot say it clearly. Prefer better names over narration.
Signatures and types are the documentation — do not duplicate them in comments.

**Never** write:
- Block comments (`/* … */`) or JSDoc-style tags (`@param`, `@returns`, `@example`)
- Blocks that restate the function, type, or file name
- "What this does" prose when the signature and body are obvious

**Do** comment (short `//` only):
- One-line godoc on exported symbols when useful: `// Suggest returns …`
- Non-obvious constraints, invariants, or trade-offs
- Why a surprising approach was chosen (not what the next line does)

```go
// ❌ BAD — narrating / block comment
/*
 * Returns path suggestions for mv/cp/cd.
 */
func (p *PathProvider) Suggest(ctx Context) []Suggestion { … }

// ✅ GOOD — no comment when the name and body are enough
func (p *PathProvider) Suggest(ctx Context) []Suggestion { … }

// ✅ GOOD — non-obvious constraint as //
// Only the token after the cursor word is completed; leave earlier args untouched.
```
